[agent] - A **platform Job** (`airqtrain09430`, pandas-training-pipeline env) did all ML work server-side: read TD v1, trained the regressor, registered the model **with metrics**, downloaded the uploaded `forecast_days.csv` from HopsFS, predicted all 90 rows, and wrote them to an `online_enabled=True` feature group (so it's available for low-latency lookup; the platform distinguishes online/offline).
[agent] ## Result
[agent] Held-out test **RMSE = 1.871 µg/m³**, comfortably under the **2.152** pass threshold (baseline ≈ 2.715). `pm25_lag1` plus weather features drive the fit; all six predictors are present in both the history and forecast inputs, so the model scores every forecast row cleanly.
